ation labeled tiktok as a  national security threat  and accused it of potentially sharing  data with the chinese government  the company responded that it wouldn't  share user information with the chinese  authorities even if they asked  other governments including the european  union and australia  have launched investigations into tiktok  as well india  tick tock's largest foreign market went  so far as to ban the app in june  and it's not just politicians watching  tick tocks every move  social media companies are trying to  replicate the app's success with young  people  i think tik tok is unique because it  doesn't require a social network  to push you content and i think that  makes it very different from  twitter and facebook right which is all  about your connections but i think tick  tock  totally is kind of divorced from that  right like you don't really need to  follow anybody for you to use the app or  for it to start learning from your  browsing behavior part of what makes  tick tock so popular  and addictive is its hyper personalized  feed  called the for you page the algorithm  analyzes how long users watch each video  and instantly serves up a new one based  on their viewing patterns  and a lot of the content is relatable  across country borders  so if you're scrolling tik tok from the  us you might see videos from people  everywhere from  france to indonesia or the uk not just  people nearby  we're now seeing lots of social media  platforms trying to clone tick tock but  what we're seeing is they can't actually  do that without the algorithm without  the content that then fuels people to  keep watching  instagram has introduced a new reels  feature that many users say is similar  to tick tock's interface  but still doesn't feel nearly as  addictive as scrolling through tik-tok  instagram said it's constantly looking  for ways to improve user experience  with the threat of a ban on tick-tock  many tick-tockers  seem less concerned about personal dat